<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="generator" content="tripline {{ card.tripline_version }}">
<title>{{ title }}</title>
<style>
:root {
  color-scheme: light;
  --bg: #f6f6f4;
  --surface: #fcfcfb;
  --surface-2: #f0efec;
  --ink: #0b0b0b;
  --ink-2: #52514e;
  --ink-3: #75746f;
  --line: #e1e0d9;
  --line-2: #c3c2b7;
  --good: #0ca30c;
  --good-ink: #006300;
  --good-tint: #e9f6e9;
  --bad: #d03b3b;
  --bad-ink: #a12525;
  --bad-tint: #fbecec;
  --pend: #8a8984;
  --pend-tint: #f3f3f1;
  --accent: #2a78d6;
  --mono: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, "Liberation Mono", monospace;
  --sans: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
}
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root {
    color-scheme: dark;
    --bg: #121211;
    --surface: #1a1a19;
    --surface-2: #232321;
    --ink: #f0efec;
    --ink-2: #c3c2b7;
    --ink-3: #9a9991;
    --line: #2c2c2a;
    --line-2: #383835;
    --good-ink: #4cc44c;
    --good-tint: #15291a;
    --bad: #e05252;
    --bad-ink: #f08080;
    --bad-tint: #321b1b;
    --pend: #8a8984;
    --pend-tint: #1f1f1e;
    --accent: #3987e5;
  }
}
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
body { margin: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); font: 14px/1.45 var(--sans); }
main { max-width: 1280px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 28px 16px 48px; }
a { color: var(--accent); }
h1 { font-size: 22px; margin: 0; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
h2 { font-size: 16px; margin: 36px 0 12px; }
.sub { color: var(--ink-2); margin: 4px 0 0; }
.mono { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.92em; }
header { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px 24px; align-items: flex-end; justify-content: space-between; }
.gate { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; padding: 6px 12px; border-radius: 999px;
  font-weight: 600; border: 1px solid; }
.gate.ok { color: var(--good-ink); background: var(--good-tint); border-color: var(--good); }
.gate.bad { color: var(--bad-ink); background: var(--bad-tint); border-color: var(--bad); }
.tiles { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(190px, 1fr)); gap: 12px; margin-top: 20px; }
.tile { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; }
.tile .k { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 12px; }
.tile .v { font-size: 28px; font-weight: 650; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin-top: 2px; }
.tile .n { color: var(--ink-3); font-size: 12px; }
.split { margin-top: 14px; background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; }
.bar { display: flex; gap: 2px; height: 12px; margin: 8px 0 8px; }
.bar span { display: block; height: 100%; border-radius: 3px; min-width: 0; }
.bar .p { background: var(--good); }
.bar .f { background: var(--bad); }
.bar .q { background: repeating-linear-gradient(45deg, var(--line-2) 0 3px, transparent 3px 6px); border: 1px solid var(--line-2); }
.legend { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px 18px; color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 12px; }
.sw { display: inline-block; width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 2px; margin-right: 6px; vertical-align: -1px; }
.sw.p { background: var(--good); } .sw.f { background: var(--bad); }
.sw.q { background: repeating-linear-gradient(45deg, var(--line-2) 0 2px, transparent 2px 4px); border: 1px solid var(--line-2); }
.matrix-wrap { overflow-x: auto; padding-bottom: 6px; }
.matrix { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat({{ columns|length }}, minmax(136px, 1fr)); gap: 10px; min-width: {{ columns|length * 146 }}px; }
.col h3 { font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: var(--ink-2); margin: 0 0 8px;
  padding-bottom: 6px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--line-2); min-height: 46px; display: flex;
  align-items: flex-end; justify-content: space-between; gap: 6px; }
.col h3 small { font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0; color: var(--ink-3); }
.cell { position: relative; background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-left: 4px solid var(--pend);
  border-radius: 8px; padding: 9px 10px 9px 10px; margin-bottom: 8px; }
.cell.passed { border-left-color: var(--good); background: var(--good-tint); }
.cell.failed { border-left-color: var(--bad); background: var(--bad-tint); }
.cell.pending { border-left-style: dashed; background: var(--pend-tint); }
.cell .tid { font-family: var(--mono); font-weight: 650; font-size: 13px; }
.cell .nm { font-size: 12.5px; margin: 2px 0 8px; color: var(--ink); }
.meta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 6px; font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--ink-2); }
.chip { border: 1px solid var(--line-2); border-radius: 4px; padding: 0 5px; font-size: 11px; color: var(--ink-2); background: var(--surface); }
.st { font-weight: 650; }
.st.passed { color: var(--good-ink); } .st.failed { color: var(--bad-ink); } .st.pending { color: var(--ink-2); }
.w { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 4px; }
.w i { display: inline-block; width: 40px; height: 5px; border-radius: 3px; background: var(--line); overflow: hidden; }
.w i b { display: block; height: 100%; background: var(--ink-2); }
details { margin-top: 6px; }
summary { cursor: pointer; font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--ink-2); }
.ev { list-style: none; margin: 6px 0 0; padding: 0; font-size: 11.5px; }
.ev li { padding: 3px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
.ev .ok { color: var(--good-ink); font-weight: 650; } .ev .no { color: var(--bad-ink); font-weight: 650; } .ev .na { color: var(--ink-3); }
.empty { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 12.5px; margin-top: 10px; }
table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden; font-size: 13px; }
th, td { text-align: left; padding: 8px 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); vertical-align: top; }
th { font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink-2); font-weight: 600; background: var(--surface-2); }
td.num, th.num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; }
.rules { margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
.rules li { white-space: nowrap; }
.failures { background: var(--bad-tint); border: 1px solid var(--bad); border-radius: 10px; padding: 10px 14px; margin-top: 14px; }
.failures ul { margin: 6px 0 0; padding-left: 18px; }
footer { margin-top: 36px; color: var(--ink-3); font-size: 12px; }
@media (max-width: 640px) { .tile .v { font-size: 24px; } }
@media print { .matrix-wrap { overflow: visible; } details { display: none; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
<header>
  <div>
    <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
    <p class="sub">Sigma rules replayed against recorded ATT&amp;CK emulation telemetry.
      Generated {{ card.generated_at.strftime("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M") }} UTC by tripline {{ card.tripline_version }}.</p>
  </div>
  {% if card.gate.passed %}
  <span class="gate ok" role="status"><span aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span> Gate passed</span>
  {% else %}
  <span class="gate bad" role="status"><span aria-hidden="true">&#10007;</span> Gate failed</span>
  {% endif %}
</header>

<section class="tiles" aria-label="Headline numbers">
  <div class="tile">
    <div class="k">Weighted coverage, all scenarios</div>
    <div class="v">{{ "%.0f"|format(totals.weighted_coverage * 100) }}%</div>
    <div class="n">pending scenarios count as zero</div>
  </div>
  {% if totals.weighted_coverage_vendored is not none %}
  <div class="tile">
    <div class="k">Weighted coverage on unmodified SigmaHQ rules alone</div>
    <div class="v">{{ "%.0f"|format(totals.weighted_coverage_vendored * 100) }}%</div>
    <div class="n">{{ totals.passed_vendored_only }} scenarios; the other {{ totals.passed_needs_authored }} passing scenarios need a rule written for this project</div>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  <div class="tile">
    <div class="k">Weighted coverage, scenarios with fixtures</div>
    <div class="v">{% if totals.weighted_coverage_scored is not none %}{{ "%.0f"|format(totals.weighted_coverage_scored * 100) }}%{% else %}n/a{% endif %}</div>
    <div class="n">{{ totals.passed + totals.failed }} of {{ totals.scenarios }} scenarios have fixtures</div>
  </div>
  <div class="tile">
    <div class="k">Scenarios</div>
    <div class="v">{{ totals.passed }}<span style="font-size:15px;color:var(--ink-3)"> / {{ totals.scenarios }} pass</span></div>
    <div class="n">{{ totals.failed }} failed, {{ totals.pending }} pending</div>
  </div>
  {% if card.benign %}
  <div class="tile">
    <div class="k">False positives, benign corpus</div>
    <div class="v">{{ card.benign.total_matches }}<span style="font-size:15px;color:var(--ink-3)"> matches</span></div>
    <div class="n">{{ card.benign.firing|length }} of {{ card.benign.evaluated|length }} evaluated rules fired on {{ card.benign.events }} benign events</div>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  {% if card.robustness %}
  <div class="tile">
    <div class="k">Evasion sweep (Linux)</div>
    <div class="v">{{ card.robustness.cmdline_any_caught }}<span style="font-size:15px;color:var(--ink-3)"> / {{ card.robustness.cmdline_total }} variants</span></div>
    <div class="n">command-line variants caught by an expected rule</div>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  <div class="tile">
    <div class="k">Expected rules</div>
    <div class="v">{{ totals.rules }}</div>
    <div class="n">{{ card.techniques|length }} techniques across {{ columns|length }} tactics</div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="split" aria-label="Prevalence weight by status">
  <div class="k" style="color:var(--ink-2);font-size:12px">Prevalence weight points ({{ split.total }} total, weight 1-10 per technique)</div>
  <div class="bar" role="img" aria-label="{{ split.passed }} passed, {{ split.failed }} failed, {{ split.pending }} pending weight points">
    {% if split.passed %}<span class="p" style="width:{{ '%.2f'|format(split.pct(split.passed)) }}%" title="passed: {{ split.passed }} points"></span>{% endif %}
    {% if split.failed %}<span class="f" style="width:{{ '%.2f'|format(split.pct(split.failed)) }}%" title="failed: {{ split.failed }} points"></span>{% endif %}
    {% if split.pending %}<span class="q" style="width:{{ '%.2f'|format(split.pct(split.pending)) }}%" title="pending: {{ split.pending }} points"></span>{% endif %}
  </div>
  <div class="legend">
    <span><i class="sw p"></i>Passed {{ split.passed }}</span>
    <span><i class="sw f"></i>Failed {{ split.failed }}</span>
    <span><i class="sw q"></i>Pending (no fixtures) {{ split.pending }}</span>
  </div>
</section>

{% if card.gate.failures %}
<section class="failures" aria-label="Gate failures">
  <strong>Gate failures</strong>
  <ul>{% for f in card.gate.failures %}<li class="mono">{{ f }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
</section>
{% endif %}

<h2>Coverage by tactic</h2>
<div class="matrix-wrap">
<div class="matrix">
{% for col in columns %}
  <div class="col">
    <h3>{{ col.label }} <small>{{ col.scenarios|length }}</small></h3>
    {% for s in col.scenarios %}
    {% set fired = s.fired_rules|length %}
    <article class="cell {{ s.status.value }}" title="{{ s.scenario_id }}">
      <div class="tid">{{ s.technique }}</div>
      <div class="nm">{{ s.name }}</div>
      <div class="meta">
        <span class="st {{ s.status.value }}">
          {%- if s.status is sameas Status.PASSED %}&#10003; Pass{% elif s.status is sameas Status.FAILED %}&#10007; Fail{% else %}&#9675; Pending{% endif -%}
        </span>
        <span class="chip">{{ planes[s.plane] }}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="meta" style="margin-top:4px">
        <span class="w" title="prevalence weight {{ s.weight }} of 10">weight {{ s.weight }} <i><b style="width:{{ s.weight * 10 }}%"></b></i></span>
      </div>
      <div class="meta" style="margin-top:4px">
        {% if s.status is sameas Status.PENDING %}rules: {{ s.expected_rules|length }} expected{% else %}rules fired: {{ fired }}/{{ s.expected_rules|length }} &middot; {{ s.events }} events{% endif %}
      </div>
      {% if s.evidence %}
      <details>
        <summary>Rule evidence</summary>
        <ul class="ev">
          {% for e in s.evidence %}
          <li>
            {% if s.status is sameas Status.PENDING %}<span class="na">&#9675;</span>{% elif e.fired %}<span class="ok">&#10003;</span>{% else %}<span class="no">&#10007;</span>{% endif %}
            {{ e.title or e.rule_id }}<br>
            <span class="na">{{ describe(e, s.events) }}</span>
          </li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </details>
      {% endif %}
    </article>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
{% endfor %}
</div>
</div>
{% if empty_tactics %}
<p class="empty">No scenarios yet: {{ empty_tactics|join(", ") }}.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2>Scenarios</h2>
<div class="table-wrap">
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Scenario</th><th>Technique</th><th>Tactic</th><th>Plane</th><th class="num">Weight</th><th>Status</th><th>Expected rules (hits / applicable events)</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for s in card.scenarios|sort(attribute="weight", reverse=true) %}
    <tr>
      <td class="mono">{{ s.scenario_id }}</td>
      <td class="mono">{{ s.technique }}</td>
      <td>{{ tactic_labels.get(s.tactic, s.tactic or "-") }}</td>
      <td>{{ planes[s.plane] }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ s.weight }}</td>
      <td><span class="st {{ s.status.value }}">{% if s.status is sameas Status.PASSED %}&#10003; Pass{% elif s.status is sameas Status.FAILED %}&#10007; Fail{% else %}&#9675; Pending{% endif %}</span></td>
      <td>
        <ul class="rules">
        {% if s.evidence %}
          {% for e in s.evidence %}
          <li>{{ e.title or e.rule_id }} <span style="color:var(--ink-3)">{% if e.outcome.value == "no_applicable_events" %}(no applicable events: routing problem){% elif e.outcome.value in ("pending", "error") %}({{ describe(e, s.events) }}){% else %}({{ e.hits }}/{{ e.evaluated }}){% endif %}</span></li>
          {% endfor %}
        {% else %}
          {% for rid in s.expected_rules %}<li>{{ rule_titles.get(rid, rid) }}</li>{% endfor %}
        {% endif %}
        </ul>
      </td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>

{% if card.benign %}
<h2>False positives on the benign corpus</h2>
<p class="sub">Every compiled rule replayed over {{ card.benign.events }} events recorded while ordinary work ran on a runner
(Linux only). Rules with no applicable benign events are listed as not evaluated, not as clean.</p>
<div class="table-wrap">
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th class="num">Matched</th><th class="num">Applicable events</th><th>Example matches</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for r in card.benign.evaluated %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ r.title }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ r.matched }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ r.applicable }}</td>
      <td class="mono">{% for e in r.examples %}{{ e }}{% if not loop.last %}<br>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p class="sub">Not evaluated (no applicable benign events): {{ card.benign.rules|length - card.benign.evaluated|length }} of {{ card.benign.rules|length }} rules.</p>
{% endif %}

{% if card.robustness %}
<h2>Evasion sweep</h2>
<p class="sub">Deterministic variants of each Linux attack command (seed {{ card.robustness.seed }}); a rule catches a variant when it
matches at least one event the variant produces. Counts are variants caught / variants the rule applies to.</p>
<div class="table-wrap">
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Scenario</th><th>Rule</th><th class="num">Command-line variants</th><th class="num">Alternative-tool variants</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for s in card.robustness.scenarios %}{% for r in s.rules %}
    <tr>
      <td class="mono">{% if loop.first %}{{ s.scenario_id }}{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{{ r.title }}{% if not r.expected %} <span style="color:var(--ink-3)">(comparison, not expected by the scenario)</span>{% endif %}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ r.cmdline_caught }} / {{ r.cmdline_variants }}</td>
      <td class="num">{% if r.alt_tool_variants %}{{ r.alt_tool_caught }} / {{ r.alt_tool_variants }}{% else %}-{% endif %}</td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}{% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>
{% endif %}

<footer>
  <p>A pass means every expected rule fired on at least one event of the scenario's recorded fixture. It is a recall
  check on one recording; the benign-corpus and evasion sections above measure false positives and robustness for the
  Linux plane only. Weight provenance (published ranking versus
  hand-assigned values) is in docs/weights.md. Source:
  <a href="https://github.com/samiali38183/tripline">github.com/samiali38183/tripline</a>.</p>
</footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
